{"version":2,"width":100,"height":28,"env":{"SHELL":"bash","TERM":"xterm-256color"},"title":"QA-Z terminal demo: catch a risky auth change before merge"}
[0.2,"o","$ pipx install git+https://github.com/qazedhq/qa-z.git\r\n"]
[0.8,"o","installed package qa-z from GitHub alpha source\r\n"]
[1.1,"o","$ qa-z init --profile python --with-agent-templates\r\n"]
[1.7,"o","created qa-z.yaml\r\ninstalled agent templates: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md\r\n"]
[2.0,"o","$ qa-z doctor\r\n"]
[2.6,"o","qa-z doctor: passed\r\nconfig: qa-z.yaml\r\nchecks: python fast gate ready\r\n"]
[2.9,"o","$ qa-z demo auth-bug\r\n"]
[3.6,"o","created isolated demo: examples/agent-auth-bug\r\nbaseline: risky auth change captured\r\ncandidate: fixed implementation included for verification\r\n"]
[3.9,"o","$ qa-z guard --from-run latest --adapter codex\r\n"]
[4.8,"o","QA-Z Guard\r\nVerdict: DO NOT MERGE YET\r\nBlocking evidence: py_test, sg_scan\r\nNext: qa-z repair-prompt --from-run latest --adapter codex\r\n"]
[5.1,"o","$ qa-z repair-prompt --from-run latest --adapter codex\r\n"]
[5.8,"o","repair prompt: .qa-z/runs/latest/repair/codex.md\r\nrepair evidence: tests failed before merge, deep auth rule flagged risk\r\n"]
